        "en": "**Paul Ricœur:** Consequently, the dichotomy between the knowing subject and the known object is a secondary abstraction that disfigures original experience.\n\n**Gabriel Marcel:** That is the capital flaw of modern epistemology. It believed it purified thought by severing the umbilical cord binding consciousness to Being.\n\n**Paul Ricœur:** This indissoluble bond between incarnation and presence indeed constitutes the unshakable departure point of your itinerary (Dialogue 1, Exchange 28)."
